interpretation.

01:00:16.420 --> 01:00:20.170
What do you think that
interpretation is?

01:00:26.480 --> 01:00:27.740
What does this say?

01:00:27.740 --> 01:00:31.620
It's saying the sum of some
things equals 0.

01:00:31.620 --> 01:00:35.080
It's saying there are some
things that if you add them up,

01:00:35.080 --> 01:00:35.940
they equal 0.

01:00:35.940 --> 01:00:39.220
But what are those things being
summed?

01:00:39.220 --> 01:00:40.480
Sum of the errors.

01:00:40.480 --> 01:00:41.640
The errors, yeah.

01:00:41.640 --> 01:00:44.120
These are just the sum of actual
minus predicted.

01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:46.500
Not squared, not absolute valued
or anything because those are

01:00:46.500 --> 01:00:48.480
all going to be non-negative, so
they're probably not going to

01:00:48.480 --> 01:00:49.580
sum to 0.

01:00:49.580 --> 01:00:52.360
But these could be positive or
negative.

01:00:52.360 --> 01:00:55.300
This is just saying the sum of
actual minus predicted

01:00:55.300 --> 01:00:59.800
if you're using the optimal line
is 0.

01:01:00.280 --> 01:01:03.000
What that tells us is whatever
line we end up finding is the

01:01:03.000 --> 01:01:04.000
